From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:17:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] feat(harmony): a switch to keep a folded phone in
 portrait

On a foldable, the HarmonyOS shell can hold the window in portrait while
the screen is phone-sized, so a tilt no longer turns a folded phone
sideways; unfolded it rotates as before. The shell owns the choice and
applies it before the page loads. General settings shows it as
"Keep portrait when folded", on foldables only, reading and changing it
through the shell's rotation.status and rotation.set.

Every other build gets the base module, which renders nothing.
